    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1014">

                <pb facs="0975" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.731/604</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-03T19:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3 1915 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 4, 10.35 a. m</hi>.]
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2223. Your 1626, May 29, and my 2209, June 1.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1014-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office now informs me that after another careful investigation, censor
                    cannot trace telegrams in question. States that British Government will <pb
                        facs="0976" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/> pass all messages between North and
                    South America sent via United Kingdom, but that such messages are liable in a
                    certain degree to be held up by accident. I suggest that persons in the United
                    States desiring to send commercial messages to South America be advised to use
                    if possible a cable route which does not touch Great Britain or her
                    possessions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
